The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': {'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': ['DISTRIBUTION_CENTERS', 'ORDERS', 'USERS', 'EVENTS', 'INVENTORY_ITEMS', 'PRODUCTS', 'ORDER_ITEMS']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• ORDER_ITEMS."status": filter rows that are exactly ‘Complete’.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."delivered_at": pick only orders whose delivery time‑stamp is before 2022 and derive YEAR / MONTH for grouping.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": monetary amount that forms the revenue per order item.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."order_id": helps count the number of completed orders (COUNT DISTINCT).  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": key used to reach product attributes.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."inventory_item_id": optional route to the per‑item manufacturing cost stored in INVENTORY_ITEMS."cost".  
• PRODUCTS."id": joins back to ORDER_ITEMS."product_id".  
• PRODUCTS."category": the product category that will be shown in the report and used in the GROUP BY clause.  
• PRODUCTS."cost": per‑unit product cost; used to aggregate total cost.  
• INVENTORY_ITEMS."cost": alternative per‑item cost when more granularity is required.  
• CONDITIONS most likely to be used  
  – ORDER_ITEMS."status" = 'Complete'  
  – ORDER_ITEMS."delivered_at" < '2022‑01‑01' (after converting the micro‑second epoch to a date or timestamp)  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (LIMIT 20 each) that gradually build understanding of the data needed for the final report.  
Every identifier is wrapped in double quotes as requested.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at the distinct order item statuses.
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Sample rows of completed order items to confirm the delivered_at values.
SELECT "order_id",
       "product_id",
       "sale_price",
       "delivered_at"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS
WHERE "status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Convert delivered_at micro‑seconds into a readable date to check the time range.
SELECT "order_id",
       TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("delivered_at"/1000000)) AS "delivered_date"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS
WHERE "status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Verify how many completed orders were delivered before 2022.
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "order_id") AS "completed_orders_before_2022"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS
WHERE "status" = 'Complete'
  AND TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("delivered_at"/1000000)) < '2022-01-01';
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: List distinct product categories that appear in completed orders.
SELECT DISTINCT P."category"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS  O
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS     P
  ON O."product_id" = P."id"
WHERE O."status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Grab some completed order items with their categories and revenue.
SELECT O."order_id",
       O."product_id",
       P."category",
       O."sale_price"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS  O
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS     P
  ON O."product_id" = P."id"
WHERE O."status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Check how product cost lines up with sale price for a random sample.
SELECT O."order_id",
       O."sale_price",
       P."cost"       AS "product_cost",
       (O."sale_price" - P."cost") AS "profit_per_item"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS  O
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS     P
  ON O."product_id" = P."id"
WHERE O."status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Monthly revenue by category (only 2021 shown as a test).
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(O."delivered_at"/1000000)) AS "month",
       P."category",
       SUM(O."sale_price") AS "revenue"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS  O
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS     P
  ON O."product_id" = P."id"
WHERE O."status" = 'Complete'
  AND DATE_TRUNC('year', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(O."delivered_at"/1000000)) = '2021-01-01'
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 1,2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Monthly cost and profit by category (test window).
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(O."delivered_at"/1000000)) AS "month",
       P."category",
       SUM(P."cost")                         AS "total_cost",
       SUM(O."sale_price")                   AS "total_revenue",
       SUM(O."sale_price") - SUM(P."cost")   AS "total_profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS  O
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS     P
  ON O."product_id" = P."id"
WHERE O."status" = 'Complete'
  AND TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(O."delivered_at"/1000000)) < '2022-01-01'
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 1,2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Demonstrate month‑over‑month growth calculations for revenue and orders.
WITH monthly AS (
  SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(O."delivered_at"/1000000)) AS "month",
         P."category",
         SUM(O."sale_price")                    AS "revenue",
         COUNT(DISTINCT O."order_id")           AS "orders"
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS  O
  JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS     P
    ON O."product_id" = P."id"
  WHERE O."status" = 'Complete'
    AND TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(O."delivered_at"/1000000)) < '2022-01-01'
  GROUP BY 1,2
)
SELECT "month",
       "category",
       "revenue",
       "orders",
       LAG("revenue") OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month") AS "prev_revenue",
       LAG("orders")  OVER (PARTITION BY "category" ORDER BY "month") AS "prev_orders",
       ROUND( ( "revenue" / NULLIF("prev_revenue",0) - 1 ) * 100 , 2) AS "pct_revenue_growth",
       ROUND( ( "orders"  / NULLIF("prev_orders",0)  - 1 ) * 100 , 2) AS "pct_order_growth"
FROM monthly
ORDER BY "category", "month"
LIMIT 20;
```
